{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1374","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Move Brackets"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a bracket sequence $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$, where $$$n$$$ is even (divisible by two). The string $$$s$$$ consists of $$$\\frac{n}{2}$$$ opening brackets '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and $$$\\frac{n}{2}$$$ closing brackets '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one move, you can choose "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly one bracket"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and move it to the beginning of the string or to the end of the string (i.e. you choose some index $$$i$$$, remove the $$$i$$$-th character of $$$s$$$ and insert it before or after all remaining characters of $$$s$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to find the minimum number of moves required to obtain "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"regular bracket sequence"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" from $$$s$$$. It can be proved that the answer always exists under the given constraints."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Recall what the regular bracket sequence is:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is regular bracket sequence; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$s$$$ is regular bracket sequence then \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" + $$$s$$$ + \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is regular bracket sequence; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$s$$$ and $$$t$$$ are regular bracket sequences then $$$s$$$ + $$$t$$$ is regular bracket sequence. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(())()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are regular bracket sequences, but \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")))"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to answer $$$t$$$ independent test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains one integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 2000$$$) — the number of test cases. Then $$$t$$$ test cases follow."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the test case contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 50$$$) — the length of $$$s$$$. It is guaranteed that $$$n$$$ is even. The second line of the test case containg the string $$$s$$$ consisting of $$$\\frac{n}{2}$$$ opening and $$$\\frac{n}{2}$$$ closing brackets."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print the answer — the minimum number of moves required to obtain "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"regular bracket sequence"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" from $$$s$$$. It can be proved that the answer always exists under the given constraints."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n2\n)(\n4\n()()\n8\n())()()(\n10\n)))((((())\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n0\n1\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case of the example, it is sufficient to move the first bracket to the end of the string."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case of the example, it is sufficient to move the last bracket to the beginning of the string."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth test case of the example, we can choose last three openning brackets, move them to the beginning of the string and obtain \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"((()))(())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1374C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1374/problem/C"}